cff-version: 1.2.0
title: VLM-imageArena
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: ansteinhuynh
abstract: >-
  An adaptive A/B image-ranking arena powered by a local vision-language
  model judge. Candidate images are compared pairwise by a VLM served via
  llama.cpp llama-server under a pinned-slot game protocol (order-
  counterbalanced queries with statistical early-exit gates), and a
  Bradley-Terry maximum-likelihood fit turns the append-only vote log into
  a reproducible ranking with confidence intervals.
keywords:
  - vision-language-model
  - llm-as-a-judge
  - bradley-terry
  - image-quality
  - llama-cpp
  - ranking
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ansteinhuynh/VLM-imageArena"
date-released: "2026-08-15"
